{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1410669-aeon-ship-naming-convention","id":1410669,"title":"Aeon Ship Naming Convention","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-27T06:35:09-07:00","id":1410669,"title":"Aeon Ship Naming Convention","content":"I'm planning to have my party leave Earth for a bit in my game. I've decided that Aeon must have a small exploration fleet. I already know that I want the ships to be named after historical members of Aeon. This will give me the opportunity to name ships after old PCs and NPCs from prior games set earlier in the timeline. What I can't decide is what letters should go infront of the name. I'm by no means a naval person, and maybe I've just watched too much Star Trek, but I want an Aeon equivalent of USS for the ships. So far I haven't come up with anything I like. I could go AEV for Aeon Exploration Vehicle, or TSV for Trinity Space Vehicle (or TSS, but that seems even worse), but I don't really like any of those. Have any of you established this convention for your games? What do you use? As best I can tell there are no references in the books.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T07:57:49-07:00","id":1410678,"title":"","content":"Here's a previous thread on naming Leviathans which might give you some inspiration: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1377453-suggested-ship-names-for-the-leviathan-jump-ships\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...han-jump-ships</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:12:32-07:00","id":1411154,"title":"","content":"So after some consideration I think I'm going to go with ATS (Aeon Trinity Ship). So the players might encounter the ATS Whitley Styles (or more likely a ship named after one of their old characters).<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:34:28-07:00","id":1411160,"title":"","content":"As far as we know, Styles is still alive and well, working behind the curtain in Aeon Trinity (there were some reports he received and sent in 1e, don\u2019t recall the book to be honest)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T07:33:07-07:00","id":1411218,"title":"","content":"I know, but (at least as far as my game is concerned) that is not a matter of public knowledge.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}